LWM <little.white.mouse@example.com> wrote:
>I have lost valks to mumaks.

So have I, back in the days when I wasn't a very good Nethack player.

Losing a valkyrie to a mumak involves one or other of operator error,
operator inexperience, or bad luck of considerable magnitude and
considerable rarity.

The relevant numbers are "five hit dice", "speed nine", and "threat
rating seven". By the time your valkyrie is meeting mumakil, she should
have some daggers with which to soften it up at range, enough hit points
to take its best shot without keeling over, enough speed to easily
outmanoeuvre it, and enough melee damage output to finish the job quickly
if the daggers don't take it down.

The effect is particularly pronounced for Lawful valkyries, given that
they start the game with two of the four prerequisites for obtaining
Excalibur (a long sword and Lawful alignment) and in normal play will
obtain the third prerequisite (XL:5) before they meet any mumakil
(absent polymorph incidents, but there are all sorts of other exciting
ways that polymorph incidents can ruin your game anyway); that leaves
only the matter of persuading the Lady of the Lake to grant you her
favour.
